{{also|Lepra}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|lepra||[[psoriasis]] & [[similar]] [[skin]] [[disease]]s}}, from {{der|en|grc-koi|λέπρα||[[psoriasis]] & [[similar]] [[skin]] [[disease]]s}}, from {{m|grc|λεπρός||[[scaly]]}}, from either {{m|grc|λεπίς||[[scale]]}} or {{m|grc|λέπος||[[husk]], [[scale]]}} + {{m|grc|-ρος||''[[form]]ing [[adjective]]s''}}. The shift of sense from [[psoriasis]] to [[Hansen's disease]] occurred in large part from the use of {{m|grc-koi|λέπρα}} to translate {{der|en|he|צרעת||[[tzaraath]]}} in the [[Septuagint]] and its subsequent use in the [[New Testament]] and [[Late Latin]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛprə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|medicine|archaic}} {{synonym of|en|leprosy}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1914|author=Henry Weightman Stelwagon|title=Treatise on Diseases of the Skin|edition=7th|page=914
|passage='''Lepra''' is an endemic, chronic, malignant, constitutional disease, due to a specific bacillus.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine|obsolete}} {{synonym of|en|psoriasis}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1864|author=William Tilbury Fox|title=Skin Diseases|page=43
|passage='''Lepra''' and [[psoriasis]] are identical, though the two names are retained.}}
# {{lb|en|botany|rare|obsolete}} [[any|Any]] [[layer]] of [[algae]], [[lichen]]s, or [[other]] [[substance]] [[producing]] a [[leprosylike]] [[appearance]] on the [[surface]]s of [[plant]]s.
#* '''1805''', translation of Karl Ludwig Willdenow as ''The Principles of Botany and of Vegetable Physiology'', p. 344:
#*: '''Lepra''' is frequently met with on the trunks, especially of young trees.

